<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 12-mth T-bill av yield falls to 22.59 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 12-mth T-bill av yield falls to 22.59 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of 12-month MKM discount Treasury bills fell to 22.59 percent at an auction on May 5 from 26.17 percent at the last auction on April 7, the National Bank said. Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   May 5		Apr 7</p>
<p> Series number		KZ4CK0705988     KZ4CK0904987</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	    400		  350</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, bln tenge)	 2.034		  1.4</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	   500		  350</p>
<p> Average price (percent)	   81.57		79.26</p>
<p> Average yield (percent)	   22.59		26.17</p>
<p> Tenor				   364 days	   364 days</p>
<p> Maturity				May 7, 1997     Apr 9, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
